contentText:
Democrats won a historic victory in the midterm elections on Tuesday (Nov. 3), flipping Congress and securing comfortable majorities in both the Senate and House of Representatives. The power shift is sure to affect policy across issues and industries, and music is no exception.

The chief area to watch come January will be congressional investigations and hearings — specifically, probes that dig into the live music sector. Democratic lawmakers are not happy with the eleventh-hour antitrust settlement reached between Live Nation and President Donald Trump’s Department of Justice (DOJ), and they’ll likely use their new gavels and subpoena powers to spotlight the president’s involvement in what they’ve called a &#8220;sweetheart deal.&#8221;

